This project borrows ideas and small pieces of code from the following MIT licensed projects.
No large blocks were copied; the relevant files carry a comment pointing back here.

hermes-live-voice (https://github.com/bielcarpi/hermes-live-voice)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Hermes Live contributors, MIT License
  - public/worklets/mic.js: the fixed-size frame-and-flush capture pattern (clients/browser/mic-worklet.js)
  - public/worklets/player.js and server/session.mjs: the idea of measuring played milliseconds on a
    barge-in and truncating the assistant transcript to what was heard (clients/browser/hermes-live-client.js)

jarvis_ai (https://github.com/eadmin2/jarvis_ai)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Chris Lassiter, MIT License
  - server/sentences.mjs: sentence extraction on terminal punctuation and the text-to-speech cleaner
    that drops think tags, replaces code blocks with a spoken placeholder and strips markdown (server/server.py)

google-adk-realtime-deepagents-example (https://github.com/langchain-ai/google-adk-realtime-deepagents-example)
  Copyright (c) LangChain, Inc., MIT License
  - public/worklets/player.js: the queue-and-drain playback worklet with a "clear" message for barge-in
    (static/pcm-player-processor.js)

